Optimal Solution - Use a single linear traversal to track and update the longest streak of consecutive 1s using a running counter.

class Solution {
    public int findMaxConsecutiveOnes(int[] nums) {
        int curr = 0;   // Tracks current streak of consecutive 1s
        int max = 0;    // Stores maximum streak found so far
        // Traverse the array
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            // If current element is 1, increase current streak
            if (nums[i] == 1) {
                curr++;
            } 
            // If element is 0, reset current streak
            else {
                curr = 0;
            }
            // Update maximum streak
            max = Math.max(max, curr);
        }
        // Return maximum consecutive 1s
        return max;
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(N).
Space Complexity :- O(1).
